    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="14" relname="nonvolitional-cause">Surely, immediate response is necessary for interactive website today.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="14" relname="span">This is one reason why many web sites such as Microsoft, AOL, Bank of America, Citigroup, etc., offer "Live chat" features.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="15" relname="span">The feature allows the customer to chat with a live customer service representative on whatever they need assistance with.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="17" relname="concession">Although, I have not used this tool,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="17" relname="span">knowing that the feature is available if I really needed help, implies that the respective company strives to cater to my needs.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="18" relname="span">For example, many banks offer live chat on their websites via pop-up dialog boxes, which inform consumers of the chat feature in order to initiate conversation.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="20" relname="span">SunTrust Banks., have been providing this feature for about two years.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="7" relname="elaboration">SunTrust's, senior vice president and managing director of SunTrust Online, John McGuire, explains, the effectiveness of live chat in saying that, ?Consumers who decline online chat do so because they are just browsing?</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="20" relname="elaboration">Those who do make contact like the service and usually complete a purchase.? (Lockyer, 2003)</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="21" relname="span">Thus, one must conclude that live chat can be effect in assisting the consumers whom need it.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="10" relname="elaboration">It provides a channel, which the customer can utilize to interact with the business.</segment>
        <group id="12" type="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
